       RowBox[{"\"\<\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[CapitalDelta]t\), \(gen\)]\)\>\"", 
        ",", " ", "\"\<mean z\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<spread z\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[54]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell["\<\
The table shows how the estimated mean and spread vary across the sampled \
noise meshes. Put the mean column in pointwise Monte Carlo standard-error \
units relative to the exact Lindblad value:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"lbz", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"lindbladBloch", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ratesB", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"initB", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
       "tfB", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"N", "[", 
         RowBox[{"tfB", "/", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
           "6", ",", " ", "12", ",", " ", "25", ",", " ", "100", ",", " ", 
            "400"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "lbz"}], "]"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "#", "]"}], "/", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "nSweep", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ",
          "/@", " ", "sweepZB"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<noise step\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<gap of the mean from Lindblad, in standard errors\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[55]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The table resolves no systematic mean bias at this sample size. The spread \
is more sensitive to the regularization mesh, as expected because the affine \
mean is diffusion-blind. A finite sweep can bound effects at its sampled \
meshes; it cannot establish the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],
 " limit."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell["A strong readout: the same route where the drift is large", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The gap between the It\[OHat] and Stratonovich drifts scales with the \
measurement rate, so a strong informative readout is the stringent test of \
feeding ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],
 " the Stratonovich form. Fix a strong readout from a tilted start, again a \
four-vector with the readout zeroed; the rates are again quantum-limited (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 "), with the intrinsic dephasing supplying the slack in the admissibility \
check:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ratesS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "7.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "4.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "1.", ",",
      " ", "3."}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"initS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0.6", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.6", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}]}],
   ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfS", " ", "=", " ", "1.5"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nS", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ratesS", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ratesS", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "<=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"2", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ratesS", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ratesS", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[56]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell["Read its efficiency:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"efficiency", "[", "ratesS", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[57]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],

Cell["Run the native reference for the strong case:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stratS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"stratRef", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ratesS", ",", " ", "initS", ",", " ", "tfS", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dtGenOf", "[", "ratesS", "]"}], ",", " ", "nS", ",", " ", 
     "3030"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[58]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],

Cell["Run the regularized ensemble for the strong case:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"regS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ensemble", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ratesS", ",", " ", "initS", ",", " ", "tfS", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dtGenOf", "[", "ratesS", "]"}], ",", " ", "nS", ",", " ", 
     "5300", ",", " ", "Automatic", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[59]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],

Cell["\<\
Compare the mean of the final Bloch vector across the three routes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"lindbladBloch", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ratesS", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"initS", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
       "tfS", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "stratS", "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "regS", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Mean of x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Mean of y\>\"", ",", "\n", 
        "    ", "\"\<Mean of z\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Lindblad\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Stratonovich\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<regularized\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[60]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the regularized mean still tracks the exact value in every \
row where the correction is large; the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],
 " row has decayed from its initial tilt toward zero under the transverse \
decay, and all three routes agree on the small residual. Compare the spread \
across the two routes:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "stratS", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "regS", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<SD of x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<SD of y\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<SD of z\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Stratonovich\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<regularized\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[61]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],

Cell["\<\
As expected, the spreads agree closely where the Stratonovich correction is \
largest. Put the sampling scale on all three components again:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"spreadGap", "[", 
     RowBox[{"stratS", ",", " ", "regS"}], "]"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\"\<Spread gap\>\"", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[62]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All three gaps sit at the sampling scale even at strong coupling. See the \
final-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 " marginal agree, the regularized histogram against the native Stratonovich \
reference:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"regS", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"stratS", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "24", 
   ",", " ", "\"\<PDF\>\"", ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<final z\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<density\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Strong readout (final value of z)\>\""}],
    ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Regularized route\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<Stratonovich ensemble\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[63]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This confirms that the regularized histogram sits on top of the native \
Stratonovich reference: the route reproduces the final-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],
 " marginal, not merely its mean, even where the drift correction is strong."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],

Cell["\<\
Repeat the finite mesh-sensitivity check in the strong-readout case, where \
the conversion correction is larger:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sweepZS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ensemble", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ratesS", ",", " ", "initS", ",", " ", "tfS", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"tfS", "/", "k"}], ",", " ", "nSweep", ",", " ", "6600", ",", 
        " ", "Automatic", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"120", ",", " ", "240", ",", " ", "480"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"N", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tfS", "/", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"120", ",", " ", "240", ",", " ", "480"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", " ", "/@", " ", "sweepZS"}]}], "}"}], 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[CapitalDelta]t\), \(gen\)]\)\>\"", 
        ",", " ", "\"\<SD in z\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[64]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],

Cell["\<\
Now read each row as a distance from the native strong-case spread, in units \
of the two estimates' sampling errors in quadrature:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"N", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tfS", "/", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"120", ",", " ", "240", ",", " ", "480"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"spreadGap", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"stratS", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}],
        " ", "/@", " ", "sweepZS"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<noise step\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<gap of the spread from the native run, in sampling errors\>\
\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[65]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],

Cell["\<\
These three estimates show no resolved trend beyond their Monte Carlo scale. \
That supports the working mesh for the displayed observable and sample size; \
it does not certify the forty-interval heuristic for other rates, initial \
states, observables, or accuracy targets.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],

Cell["What is now true", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The monitored qubit and its accumulated readout form one four-component SDE \
driven by one scalar noise. To make an equation ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],
 " can accept, first convert the target It\[OHat] drift to the equivalent \
Stratonovich drift, then replace the Wiener path by a continuous \
piecewise-cubic approximation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],
 " receives the random ODE ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], "."], 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Strat",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],
 ". Under the scalar-noise Wong-Zakai conditions, its solution approaches the \
target It\[OHat] process through the equivalent Stratonovich representation \
as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],

Cell["\<\
The exact algebra is stronger than the numerical evidence: the It\[OHat] \
conversion, Lindblad generator, readout identity, and Bloch-ball flux all \
reduce symbolically to the claimed formulas. The simulations are \
finite-resolution checks. Their means and spreads agree with the stated \
references at the displayed scales, but regularization bias, \
stochastic-integrator bias, ODE error, and Monte Carlo uncertainty remain \
distinct error sources.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Integrating the readout beside the state costs one extra equation and \
preserves the shared innovation explicitly. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],
 ", its ensemble mean is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"C", "I"}], "TI"]]], 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],
 "; subtracting the pathwise signal returns the same regularized Wiener path \
that drives the state; and with drive and relaxation absent, the monitored \
coordinate is a closed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["tanh",
   FontSlant->"Plain"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],
 " function of the record. The Bloch-vector interpretation requires ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"C", "I"}], "TI"]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"B", "A"}], "TI"]], "\[LessEqual]", "2", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],
 "; outside that condition the equation may still integrate, but its \
trajectories need not represent density matrices."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"
]
